Catalog number : I00043
Uniform title: Śivagaṇapatisubrahmaṇyapratiṣṭhā
Manuscript : IFP manuscript bundle RE30970
Description: RE30970. This bundle titled as Śiva-Gaṇapati-Subrahmaṇyapratiṣṭhā, (शिवगणपतिसुब्रह्मण्य-प्रतिष्ठा), it encompasses a detailed exploration of consecration rituals for Lord Śiva, Lord Gaṇapati, and Lord Subrahmaṇya. It begins with the Samprokṣaṇavidhi (ritual on purification) from Śrīmadaṃśumattantra and continues with the pratiṣṭhā chapters for Lord Śiva, derived from Śivālayanirmāṇadīpikā. The pratiṣṭhā chapters for Lord Subrahmaṇya are sourced from Kumāratantra, while the pratiṣṭhā chapters for Lord Gaṇapati are taken from Śrīmaccandrajñānāgama. Together, these texts offer a comprehensive guide to temple construction and deity consecration, emphasizing the unique procedures and symbolic rituals associated with each deity.The bundle contains 109 folios and there are 5-8 lines in each folio. The size of the folio is 39x3.3 mm. This manuscript is an invaluable resource for understanding the Āgamic principles and rituals surrounding deity consecration, drawing from significant Tantras and Āgamas. Its blend of ritualistic and architectural details makes it an essential reference for practitioners and scholars of Hindu temple traditions on the Āgamas.
